["The Kretschmann scalar $K$ of the extreme Kerr throat against $\\theta$ ($r_0 = 1$), the same at every radius, time, and $\\phi$.","$K$ vanishes at both poles and at $\\theta_0$ and $\\pi - \\theta_0$, where $\\theta_0 = \\arccos(2 - \\sqrt{3})$. It is negative between each pole and the nearer of these angles, and positive between them. On the equator it is greatest, $192/r_0^4$, and it is finite at every angle. Its least value is $-92.527/r_0^4$, at $\\theta = 0.340\\pi$ and $0.660\\pi$.","The throat is a vacuum, so the Ricci scalar vanishes."],"settings":"$r_0 = 1$, the unit of every length, with $0 \\le \\theta \\le \\pi$ from pole to pole and $\\theta_0 = \\arccos(2 - \\sqrt{3})$ the angle of the first interior zero of $K$.","clip":"We draw $K\\,r_0^4$ on a signed linear scale from $-100$ to $200$, with no value clipped."}]}
